<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ionian Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">499–493 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ionian Revolt was a rising of the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a> and other parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> against Persian rule, from 499 to 493 BCE. Led at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristagoras-of-miletus">Aristagoras of Miletus</a> and supported briefly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and Eretria, it ended after the Persian naval victory at Lade and the sack of Miletus in 494 BCE. It led to the Persian invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt.jpg" alt="Ionian Revolt" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ionian_Revolt_Campaign_Map-fr.svg: Eric Gaba (Sting - fr:Sting) derivative work: MinisterForBadTimes (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ionian_Revolt_Campaign_Map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
